## Non-functional targets

| Concern | Initial target |
|---|---|
| Initial JavaScript | <= 200 KB gzipped on the main route |
| LCP / INP / CLS | < 2.5 s / < 200 ms / < 0.1 |
| Accessibility | WCAG 2.2 AA |

## Observability

- **Client errors:** one reporting sink; include route, release, and request ID.
- **Web vitals:** report LCP, INP, and CLS per route.
- **Build output:** enforce a bundle-size budget in CI.

## Deployment

Build static assets and serve them from a CDN with immutable, content-hashed
filenames. Do not cache the HTML entry for long.

## Known risks and trade-offs

- The API contract can change without this repository noticing; regenerate
  types in CI and fail on drift.
- Client-side checks are only for usability; the service enforces every rule.
- Bundle growth is mitigated by route-level code splitting and a CI size budget.

